    "memoText": "\n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 586\n\nTO THE SENATE:\n\nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n\nSenate Bill Number 7706, entitled:\n\n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend  the  insurance law, in relation to insurance on\n      wireless communications equipment\"\n\n    NOT APPROVED\n\n  This bill would amend  the  Insurance  Law  to  limit  the  disclosure\nrequirements  for  wireless communications equipment insurance that must\nbe provided to consumers at the point of sale.\n\n  Over the last three years, I have vetoed similar bills that  similarly\ndiluted existing consumer protections by limiting the required insurance\ndisclosures provided to consumers who purchase these devices. This bill,\nunfortunately,   suffers  from  the  same  flaws,  and  I  therefore  am\nconstrained to disapprove it.\n\n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n\n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
